# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Nothing here is read at import time --
# only `auth.load_dotenv()` reads it, and real environment variables always win.
#
# This project never places orders, so none of the order-placement prerequisites
# (static IP registration, an app secret for the OAuth consent flow) are needed.
# See src/bnfmm/data/auth.py and tests/test_no_order_placement.py.
#
# ON THE DHANHQ DEVELOPER PORTAL (Live Environment page), most of what is offered
# is for capabilities this project does not have. Named explicitly because three
# of the four fields there are easy to mistake for the ones below:
#   - "API Key" / "API Secret"  -- drives the OAuth *consent* flow
#     (DhanLogin.generate_login_session / consume_token_id). Not used here: the
#     PIN+TOTP endpoint takes dhanClientId, pin and totp and nothing else.
#   - "Postback URL"            -- order webhooks. Nothing to receive.
#   - "Static IP settings"      -- an order-placement prerequisite. Leave unset;
#     the portal only lets an IP be re-set once every 7 days, so a stray edit is
#     expensive to undo.
# The only things worth taking from that page are the client id and, if you use
# the manual path, a freshly generated access token.

# Your Dhan client id: the numeric login/UCC id, from the portal Dashboard or the
# Dhan app under Profile. NOT the API Key, and NOT the Application Name given to
# a generated token.
BNFMM_DHAN_CLIENT_ID=

# The PIN used at login -- the same one typed into the Dhan app. Not a portal
# artifact. Required to mint a token via the TOTP path.
BNFMM_DHAN_PIN=

# Base32 TOTP seed, from when the authenticator was enrolled for this account.
# OPTIONAL -- leave it blank and you are prompted for the six digits each session,
# which keeps the seed off this machine entirely.
BNFMM_TOTP_SECRET=

# OPTIONAL alternative to the three above: paste a token minted elsewhere (the
# portal's "Generate Token", a separate script) and no PIN or TOTP is needed.
#
# Mind the expiry. The portal's My Tokens table shows a "Time to Expiry" per
# token, and a token pasted the night before a session can be dead by the open --
# check the remaining hours cover 09:00-15:35 IST, or generate a fresh one in the
# morning. The PIN+TOTP path above mints per run and does not have this failure
# mode, which is why it is the default.
BNFMM_DHAN_ACCESS_TOKEN=
